      {
        "type": "Module",
        "name": "usb_uart_bridge",
        "description": "CH340 USB-to-UART bridge interfaces the USB data pair to a UART endpoint and exposes board-level TXD and RXD signals. The module consumes the internally generated VCC_3V3 rail for logic power distribution intent. USB UD_P and UD_N are the upstream USB interface. UART data direction must be preserved: CH340 TXD is the board transmit output and CH340 RXD is the board receive input. Handshake and modem-control related pins CTS, DSR, RI, DCD, DTR, RTS plus R232 are present on the device but are not required by the brief, so they should remain intentionally uncommitted or be given explicit default treatment during downstream wiring rather than assumed active use. XI and XO indicate the clock-related interface and must be handled according to the actual CH340 variant support requirements in downstream design without guessing unsupported topology here. V3 is a device-specific rail/interface pin and should be connected only according to authoritative CH340 requirements during later schematic work.",
        "id": "usb_uart_bridge"
      },
